  "text": "Classic Neapolitan ice cream is a delightful combination of three flavors: vanilla, chocolate, and strawberry. Since you asked for a simple recipe, here's a straightforward version you can make at home:\n\n---\n\n### **Classic Neapolitan Ice Cream (Vanilla, Chocolate, Strawberry) \u2013 Simple Recipe**\n\n#### **Ingredients:**\n\n- **For the base (sugar, milk, cream, egg yolks):**\n  - 2 cups (480 ml) full-fat milk\n  - 1 cup (240 ml) heavy cream\n  - 3/4 cup (60 g) granulated sugar\n  - 2 tablespoons (30 ml) all-purpose flour (to thicken)\n  - 3 large egg yolks\n  - 1 vanilla bean (or 1 teaspoon vanilla extract)\n  - A pinch of salt\n\n- **For the flavors:**\n  - **Vanilla Ice Cream**: 1 cup (240 ml) vanilla ice cream mix or additional milk, cream, egg yolks, and sugar (follow the base recipe and add vanilla)\n  - **Chocolate Ice Cream**: 1 cup (240 ml) chocolate ice cream mix or additional milk, cream, egg yolks, sugar, and melted dark chocolate (use 1/2 cup chocolate)\n  - **Strawberry Ice Cream**: 1 cup (240 ml) strawberry puree (fresh or frozen), 1/2 cup (120 ml) milk, 2 tablespoons (30 ml) sugar, and 1/2 vanilla bean or extract (optional)\n\n---\n\n### **Instructions:**\n\n1. **Make the Base:**\n   - In a medium saucepan, combine milk, cream, sugar, flour, egg yolks, vanilla, and salt.\n   - Whisk until smooth and steaming hot (about 160\u00b0F / 70\u00b0C).\n   - Pour into a clean bowl and let cool for 15\u201320 minutes.\n   - Chill the base in the refrigerator for 1 hour or until very cold.\n\n2. **Make the Flavors:**\n   - **Vanilla**: Follow the base recipe, but instead of chocolate or strawberry, use vanilla extract.\n   - **Chocolate**: Use the base recipe and add 1/2 cup melted dark chocolate (stirring until melted).\n   - **Strawberry**: Blend 1 cup fresh strawberries (or frozen, thawed) with 1/2 cup milk, 2 tablespoons sugar, and 1/2 vanilla bean (or extract). Chill.\n\n3. **Churn:**\n   - Pour each flavor into separate portions (approx. 1/3 each).\n   - Churn in an ice cream maker according to the manufacturer's instructions, usually 20\u201325 minutes, until soft-serve consistency is reached.\n\n4. **Freeze:**\n   - Transfer the mixtures to airtight containers and freeze for at least 2 hours to firm up.\n\n---\n\n### **Enjoy:**\nServe in a small cup or cone with a spoon, taking one flavor at a time. The traditional way is to eat one scoop of each and mix them together.\n\nLet me know if you'd like a version without an ice cream maker or want a no-churn option! \ud83c\udf66",
